2012-11-20  Havard Eidnes <he@uninett.no>

	* traffic/report/tail-stats.pl: Several changes rolled up into one:
	 * Change from piping into rrdtool to using the perl RRDs module.
	 * Improve some diagnostic output to include more information.
	 * Try as carefully as possible to not trigger any error messages when
	   doing RRD update operations, by checking for the last update time
	   and skipping any later samples, and also checking that the sample
	   times are monotonically increasing (violations will be skipped)
	 * Fix a bug where values from a prior data file read would "shine
	   through", e.g. when the new device doesn't do 64-bit counters; in
	   that case the old values would lie lingering about, causing "data
	   rate exceeds ifspeed" errors.  (I really, really ought to re-write
	   the interface to the central "read raw data" routines...)
	 * Make it possible to process historical data files in parallel via
	   the "-j" option.  This is useful if you have sufficient I/O
	   capacity and several CPU cores.
	 * In order to avoid attempts to update data for same logical port
	   more than once, weed out duplicates (and emit a warning) before
	   doing the processing.

	* traffic/report/rr-test.pl:
	Expand this to a test comparing data rates with ifspeed,
	and automatic detection of 64-bit octet counters.

	* traffic/cgi/r-all.pl:
	&err() may be called before $q is initialized, so check for it and
	initialize before using it.

