2012-11-10  Havard Eidnes <he@uninett.no>

	* ChangeLog, Makefile: Mark this as 0.9.9.7.

	* traffic/common/read-raw-log.pl:
	Thanks to Ville Mattila at CSC who found that the code was using
	an undefined $pos if the optional $td argument (indicating how
	close to the start time of the script to read the data) isn't supplied.
	Instead, always record the current position; if we're incrementally
	reading new-format files, the second test for "new format" will hit,
	and we need to re-position so that new_read_log() will se the current
	line again.

	The net effect is a speed-up of the incremental reading and processing
	of the data; not always reading from the start of the file(!)

