2011-05-25  Havard Eidnes <he@uninett.no>

	* INSTALL: Add p5-BerkeleyDB as a requirement.

	* traffic/db/update-dbs.pl, traffic/db/update-close.pl,
	traffic/db/bdb-load.pl, traffic/db/bdb-dump.pl,
	traffic/db/db-lookup.pl:
	Implement BerkeleyDB as a preferred alternative to the original "bdm"
	hashed files (which are BerkeleyDB version 1, in all probability).  If
	database files named ntf.bdb and ftn.bdb exists, they will be
	preferred over the older "dbm" hashed files, and accessed using the
	BerkeleyDB perl module.

	This is done because at least one installation of zino has hit a bug
	or a limitation in the original "dbm" implementation, causing a
	segfault with perl 5.8 and a perl-internal panic with perl 5.12, both
	of which are avoided if using BerkeleyDB with version 4 DB library and
	databases.

	Convert to ntf.bdb and ftn.bdb by using "../bin/dbm-dump ftn > ftn"
	and subsequently "../bin/bdb-load ftn.bdb ftn", which will create the
	ftn.bdb database, and correspondingly for the ntf database.

