2010-09-24  Havard Eidnes <he@uninett.no>

	* tpoller/tpoller.tcl:
	Change to a new raw data format where we log time stamps as seconds
	since Jan 1 1970 00:00:00 UTC instead of as a string in the local time
	zone.  The latter has been the source of much teeth-gnashing over DST-
	related bugs, particularly when the raw data files are processed
	incrementally in "tail" mode.  Those bugs should now be history.

	* tpoller/Makefile: Add new files which are now included in zino.

	* zinomon/Makefile:
	Avoid referring to ${PROGS} so as to not interfere with the default
	.mk setup on NetBSD.

	* zino/swalk.tcl:
	Extend swalk so that it can optionally take names of functions to
	call at end-of-table and in case of an error event.

	* vwatch/Makefile:
	Avoid problems with using macros with predefined meaning in NetBSD's
	make setup.  Someday we ought to consider autoconfig'ing this stuff
	and not use NetBSD's .mk files at all...

	* traffic/report/tail-stats.pl:
	Make it possible to only process a subset of logical ports
	via the -n option, also for "today".
	Also print an error message instead of an error code if rrd fails.

	* traffic/report/report-day.pl:
	Make this run with "use strict;" which actually improves performance
	radically with a newish perl.

	* traffic/report/customer-ts.pl:
	Add some debugging code active under -V.  Make sure to print times in
	hh:mm:ss format in local time.

	* traffic/jobs/Makefile: Add the new files to be installed.

	* traffic/jobs/onlyone.sh: Add a comment.

	* traffic/jobs/fixup-data.pl:
	Add detection of the new raw data format, and add a function to deal
	with that format.

	* traffic/jobs/compress-data.pl:
	Make the daily compression job able to handle lots of files by using
	find + xargs.

	* traffic/common/date.pl:
	Correctly compute the number of days in a year, accounting for leap
	years.

	* traffic/common/Makefile: Add the new scripts to be installed.

	* traffic/common/read-raw-log.pl, traffic/common/read-hr-log.pl:
	Detect the new version format, and switch to the routine reading that
	format.

	* traffic/common/read-5m-sum.pl:
	Disable DST compensation when reading new-style raw data logs,
	since the new code's use of %lasttime is different than the old.

	* ritz/notify.tcl: Get rid of an un-needed declaration.

	* traffic/cgi/r-all.pl:
	If, for some reason, the desc file is unreadable or nonexistent, emit
	an error to that effect (usually a config error).

	* traffic/common/new-read-hr-log.pl, traffic/common/new-read-raw-log.pl:
	Add a variant of the read-raw-log script which processes new-style
	timestamped raw data files, where timestamps are in seconds since 1
	Jan 1970 00:00:00 UTC.  Gone should therefore be bugs in the DST
	handling code, which were especially troublesome for incremental file
	processing.

	* traffic/common/dst-test.pl:
	Add a small script which parses an old-style date timestamp on input
	and prints whether the given day goes from or to DST.  This should now
	be redundant, since we log with time stamps in UTC.

	* traffic/jobs/split-new-data.pl:
	Add a script which can split new-style raw data files over days.
	I'm not entirely satisfied with the way the arguments are handled,
	maybe it will improve in the next iteration.

	* traffic/jobs/check-deltas.pl:
	Add a small debugging script (not installed) which checks the
	time-delta values in the data file.  This turns out to have limited
	usefulness for historical logs, because there intermediate lines
	with the same value have been filtered out.

	* traffic/jobs/print-old.pl:
	Add a small debugging script (not installed), which prints
	the time stamps in the old style.

	* traffic/jobs/convert-data.pl:
	Add a script which will convert from old-style to new-style time
	stamps in the raw data files.

	* traffic/jobs/daily.pl:
	Make the daily job able to handle lots of files by using find +
	xargs and the recently added move-to and copy-to scripts.
	This should make the daily job able to handle lots of files,
	and avoids relying on the maximum command line length.

	* traffic/jobs/copy-to:
	Add a script for copying a set of files to a given directory, suitable
	for use with find and xargs.

	* traffic/jobs/move-to:
	Add a script to move a set of files to a given directory,
	suitable for use with find and xargs.

	* zinomon/Makefile:
	Avoid the use of PROGS, use variants so as to not conflict with
	NetBSD's mk rules.

	* vwatch/Makefile:
	Avoid problems with using macros with predefined meaning in NetBSD's
	make setup.  Someday we ought to consider autoconfig'ing this stuff
	and not use NetBSD's .mk files at all...

	* traffic/report/customer-ts.pl:
	Add some more debug output, and ensure times printed in debug output
	are in local time.

	* traffic/common/new-read-raw-log.pl:
	We need to remember the position we had progressed to for each round.

	* traffic/cgi/r-all.pl:
	Emit a warning if description file can't be opened.

