2009-10-23  Havard Eidnes <he@uninett.no>

	* traffic/cgi/r-all.pl:
	If we got an error during RRD-graphing, print it together with
	the RRD-graph arguments to stderr, ends up in apache's error log.

	Correct the font specification: there is no need for single quoting,
	and it actually nulls out the font selection(!)

	Also, be less specific about the legend font, and let rrdtool pick a
	suitable monospace font (it defaults to monospace).

	* traffic/cgi/r-all.pl:
	Drop a superflous newline from an error message.

	* traffic/cgi/r-all.pl:
	Get rid of a tab in the legend.  It frequently pushed the end of the
	line to wrap, causing different-sized images to be created.  This in
	turn could cause overflow in the %img_size hash, because it's tied to
	a fixed-size shared memory segment, defaulting (in my case) to 64KB.

	Also protect the statements which add an exception to the %img_size
	hash, so that if we try to exceed the shared memory segment size, the
	error is not fatal.  Instead, emit a message in the error log, and
	continue on.  The price to pay is to have the web client stretch or
	compress the images, which may not look so pretty.

	Ideally, we ought to figure out a better way of dimensioning the
	shared memory segment, so that it's less likely to overflow.  We also
	ought to devise a way to have the general image size be out-voted by
	the number of exceptions for the given type of plot...

