	by initializing $p to our current "root".
	During data processing, if we get delta_t=0, skip sample.

	Make two functions to save and merge back in saved values.  This is to
	fix problems which occur when you have data from many sources, and
	they are collected asynchronously, and a few samples spill into the
	"next" sample.  Saving a few samples lets us smooth over what would
	otherwise be a "ragged edge".

	Also introduce a configurable time-delay so that we stop reading data
	sources when "now - time-dalay" is found.  This was an earlier attempt
	at avoiding the problem fixed by the save+merge functions above, and
	may now actually be redudant.  However, "don't change something which
	works" will be the motto for now.

	Always save 2 samples worth of data and merge it back when we're
	re-run.

