2007-09-06  Havard Eidnes <he@uninett.no>

	* zino/status.tcl: Comment out some debug logging.

	* zino/trap.tcl: Add the SNMPv2 BGP backward transition notification.
	Ignore it for now.

	* zino/zino-main.tcl:
	Use the poll scheduler instead of polling directly.

	* zino/bgp.tcl:
	Mark the last activity in the table walker for the benefit of the poll
	scheduler / rate limiter.

	* zino/status.tcl:
	Insert a scheduler between the config file + job scheduler and the
	actual router polls.  This ensures that router polls are better
	spread out (prevents "clustering" of polls) and that there is a
	minimum of 60 seconds between the last activity towards a router
	and the start of a new poll.

	To this end, each of the table walkers which are done as part of
	the router poll have been instrumented to mark when the last
	activity was being done.

	Also, replace use of regexp with simple string equality comparison
	when that is sufficient.

	Since SNMP callbacks are evaluated in the global context(!), make
	sure to invoke a procedure to handle things which might require the
	use of local variables.  Such variables directly in the SNMP callback
	will end up as global variables(!), and this can mess things up
	royally if the variable values are used to direct the polling.

